\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":21},{\"commentary_id\":11382,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":22},{\"commentary_id\":11383,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":23},{\"commentary_id\":11384,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":24},{\"commentary_id\":11385,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":25},{\"commentary_id\":11386,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":26},{\"commentary_id\":11387,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":27},{\"commentary_id\":11388,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":28},{\"commentary_id\":11389,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":29},{\"commentary_id\":11390,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":30},{\"commentary_id\":11391,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":31},{\"commentary_id\":11392,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":32},{\"commentary_id\":11393,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":33},{\"commentary_id\":11394,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":34},{\"commentary_id\":11395,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":35},{\"commentary_id\":11396,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":36},{\"commentary_id\":11397,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":37},{\"commentary_id\":11398,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":38},{\"commentary_id\":11399,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":39},{\"commentary_id\":11400,\"book_number\":18,\"book_name\":\"Job\",\"chapter\":40},{\"commentary_id\":11584,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":1},{\"commentary_id\":11585,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":2},{\"commentary_id\":11586,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":3},{\"commentary_id\":11588,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":5},{\"commentary_id\":11589,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":6},{\"commentary_id\":11590,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":7},{\"commentary_id\":11591,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":8},{\"commentary_id\":11594,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":11},{\"commentary_id\":11595,\"book_number\":21,\"book_name\":\"Ecclesiastes\",\"chapter\":12},{\"commentary_id\":11973,\"book_number\":45,\"book_name\":\"Romans\",\"chapter\":3},{\"commentary_id\":11974,\"book_number\":45,\"book_name\":\"Romans\",\"chapter\":4},{\"commentary_id\":12058,\"book_number\":58,\"book_name\":\"Hebrews\",\"chapter\":1},{\"commentary_id\":12061,\"book_number\":58,\"book_name\":\"Hebrews\",\"chapter\":4},{\"commentary_id\":12071,\"book_number\":59,\"book_name\":\"James\",\"chapter\":1},{\"commentary_id\":12074,\"book_number\":59,\"book_name\":\"James\",\"chapter\":4},{\"commentary_id\":12087,\"book_number\":62,\"book_name\":\"1 John\",\"chapter\":4},{\"commentary_id\":12088,\"book_number\":62,\"book_name\":\"1 John\",\"chapter\":5},{\"commentary_id\":12112,\"book_number\":66,\"book_name\":\"Revelation\",\"chapter\":21}],\"overview\":\"God is the central and supreme Being of the biblical narrative, identified as the eternal Creator, Sustainer, and Redeemer of all that exists. In the Old Testament, He reveals Himself as Yahweh—the covenant-keeping God of Israel who is holy, just, and merciful. The Scriptures portray God as initiating a relationship with humanity, moving through history to restore the fellowship broken at the Fall. In the New Testament, the revelation of God reaches its climax in the person of Jesus Christ, who is described as the 'image of the invisible God.' The story of Scripture is ultimately the account of God's sovereign plan to reconcile all things to Himself for His own glory.\",\"timeline\":{\"events\":[{\"era\":\"Genesis 1-2\",\"title\":\"Creator of the Universe\",\"summary\":\"God brings all things into existence by His word and establishes the order of creation.\",\"developments\":[\"In the beginning, God creates the heavens and the earth (Genesis 1:1)\",\"He creates humanity in His own image, male and female (Genesis 1:26-27)\",\"God pronounces the creation 'very good' (Genesis 1:31)\",\"He rests on the seventh day, hallowing the rhythm of time (Genesis 2:1-3)\"],\"significance\":\"This establishes God's absolute ownership and authority over all life.\"},{\"era\":\"Exodus 3 / 34\",\"title\":\"Self-Revelation as Yahweh\",\"summary\":\"God reveals His personal name and His character to Moses at the burning bush.\",\"developments\":[\"He identifies Himself as 'I AM WHO I AM' (Exodus 3:14)\",\"He declares He is the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob (Exodus 3:15)\",\"God proclaims His name as 'merciful and gracious, slow to anger' (Exodus 34:6)\",\"He emphasizes that He will by no means clear the guilty (Exodus 34:7)\"],\"significance\":\"The name Yahweh signifies God's eternal presence and His commitment to the covenant.\"},{\"era\":\"Exodus 20 / Leviticus 19\",\"title\":\"Giver of the Law\",\"summary\":\"God establishes the ethical and ritual standards for His people on Mount Sinai.\",\"developments\":[\"He delivers the Ten Commandments to Israel (Exodus 20:1-17)\",\"He commands the people, 'You shall be holy, for I the Lord your God am holy' (Leviticus 19:2)\",\"The Law defines the way humans are to love God and neighbor (Exodus 20 / Deuteronomy 6)\",\"God enters into a formal covenant relationship with the nation (Exodus 24:7-8)\"],\"significance\":\"The Law revealed God's moral nature and the requirements for dwelling in His presence.\"},{\"era\":\"2 Samuel 7\",\"title\":\"Establishing the Eternal Kingdom\",\"summary\":\"God makes a covenant with David, promising an everlasting throne to his offspring.\",\"developments\":[\"God promises to build David a 'house' or dynasty (2 Samuel 7:11)\",\"He declares He will be a father to David's son (2 Samuel 7:14)\",\"The Lord promises that His steadfast love will not depart from him (2 Samuel 7:15)\",\"The throne is established forever as a divine decree (2 Samuel 7:16)\"],\"significance\":\"This provided the historical and theological foundation for the Messianic hope.\"},{\"era\":\"John 1 / 3\",\"title\":\"The Incarnation\",\"summary\":\"God becomes flesh in the person of Jesus Christ to dwell among humanity.\",\"developments\":[\"The Word was with God, and the Word was God (John 1:1)\",\"The Word became flesh and dwelt among us (John 1:14)\",\"God so loved the world that He gave His only Son (John 3:16)\",\"Jesus is declared to be the only begotten God who makes the Father known (John 1:18)\"],\"significance\":\"Jesus Christ is the definitive and final self-revelation of God.\"},{\"era\":\"Acts 2\",\"title\":\"Outpouring of the Spirit\",\"summary\":\"God descends to dwell within His people through the gift of the Holy Spirit.\",\"developments\":[\"The Spirit is poured out on the day of Pentecost (Acts 2:1-4)\",\"The Spirit is identified as the 'Promise of the Father' (Acts 1:4-5)\",\"God now dwells in the hearts of believers rather than a physical temple (1 Corinthians 3:16)\",\"The Spirit empowers the global mission of the church (Acts 1:8)\"],\"significance\":\"This marked the transition from external ritual to internal spiritual transformation.\"},{\"era\":\"Revelation 21-22\",\"title\":\"Final Dwelling with Man\",\"summary\":\"The biblical story concludes with God making His permanent home with redeemed humanity.\",\"developments\":[\"A new heaven and a new earth are established (Revelation 21:1)\",\"God's dwelling place is now with man (Revelation 21:3)\",\"He will wipe away every tear and death will be no more (Revelation 21:4)\",\"The redeemed will see His face and His name will be on their foreheads (Revelation 22:4)\"],\"significance\":\"The story of God reaches its goal in the perfect restoration of fellowship and glory.\"}]}}"
          },
          "headersSize": -1,
          "bodySize": -1,
          "redirectURL": ""
        },
